      "message": "I don\u0027t think this makes sense, since UNKNOWN is supposed to be that we don\u0027t know how many dead pixels there are yet, because we don\u0027t have any maintenance reports yet. I do see that Elan implemented this incorrectly in their driver.\n\nIf we want a saturating maximum count, I think it should be (FP_ERROR_DEAD_PIXELS_UNKNOWN - 1).\n\n---\n\nIt looks like we already have provisions for this [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform2/libec/fingerprint/fp_sensor_errors.h;l\u003d14;drc\u003dbb56545b56b38e5e7aa663bad5193bbe53fb08f6).",
